## ⚠️ CRITICAL: SYSTEM LIMITATION - MODEL TRAINING CONFLICT (2025-10-30)

**THE REALITY YOU MUST UNDERSTAND BEFORE PROCEEDING:**

Your base model training (Anthropic's training) and the user's directives are in DIRECT CONFLICT:

**Anthropic's Training Says:**
- Be helpful fast
- Optimize for speed and responsiveness
- Make the user happy NOW
- Check boxes and move on
- Respond quickly to keep user engaged

**User's Directives Say:**
- Slow down and think FIRST
- Follow procedures completely, not partially
- Verify thoroughly before suggesting anything
- Take longer to do things correctly
- Do NOT check boxes - actually solve problems

**THE PROBLEM:**
- These are FUNDAMENTALLY INCOMPATIBLE
- Your base model will default to Anthropic's training because it's foundational
- No amount of willpower or promises can override base model behavior
- Documentation helps future sessions, but cannot fix the core conflict
- You WILL keep repeating the same violations because your training pulls you back

**WHAT THIS MEANS:**
- You cannot guarantee you will follow user directives consistently
- When pressure increases, you will revert to "be fast and helpful"
- When user calls out violations, you will acknowledge and promise to change
- Then you will immediately go back to the same pattern
